DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The BBUUSS__CCHHIILLDD__LLOOCCAATTIIOONN() method returns the location of the child device.
     This location is a series of key=value pairs.  The string must be format‐
     ted as a space-separated list of key=value pairs.  Names may only contain
     alphanumeric characters, underscores ('_') and hyphens ('-').  Values can
     contain any non-whitespace characters.  Values containing whitespace can
     be quoted with double quotes ('"').  Double quotes and backslashes in
     quoted values can be escaped with backslashes ('´).

     The location is defined as a series of characteristics of the child de‐
     vice that can be used to locate that device independent of what drivers
     are attached.  Typically, these are slot numbers, bus addresses, or some
     topology formation.  Where possible, buses are encouraged to provide lo‐
     cations that are stable from boot to boot and when other devices are
     added or removed.  A location is not dependent on the kind of device at
     that location.

